    <statement><p>Rewrite the following expression into the form of a+b<m>i</m>:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{{-6+2i}}{{1-i}} = }</m><fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4-2i</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>By definition, <m>i=\sqrt{-1}</m>, so we have <m>i^{2}=-1</m>.</p>
<p>To get rid of <alert><m>i</m></alert> in the denominator, we use the difference of squares formula:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
 \begin{aligned}
   \amp \phantom{{}=}(1+{-i})(1-{-i}) \\
   \amp = (1)^{2}-({-i})^{2} \\
   \amp = (1)-(-1) \\
   \amp = 2
 \end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>The full solution is:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}
   \amp \phantom{{}=} \frac{{-6+2i}}{{1-i}} \\
   \amp = \frac{({-6+2i})(1-{-i})}{({1-i})(1-{-i})}  \\
   \amp = \frac{(-6)(1)+(-6)(-{-i})+({2i})(1)+({2i})(-{-i})}{2}  \\
   \amp = \frac{(-6)+(-6i)+(2i)+(2)(i^{2})}{2}  \\
   \amp = \frac{(-6)+(-4i)+(2)(-1)}{2}  \\
   \amp = \frac{(-6)+(-4i)+(-2)}{2}  \\
   \amp = \frac{(-8)+(-4i)}{2}  \\
   \amp = \frac{-8}{2}+\frac{-4i}{2}  \\
   \amp = {-4-2i}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
</solution>
